 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot P)$ per ray, where $N$ is the number of samples and $P$ is the cost of the MLP query [S13]. Training is computationally expensive, requiring high computing power and long times [S13].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N \cdot B)$ for storing intermediate tensors (sigma, rgb, weights) for a batch of size $B$ [S7, unofficial][S9].
 *   **Measured Performance:** Original NeRF is slow; Instant NGP reduces processing time significantly using multi-resolution hash encoding [S13]. HeadNeRF achieves >40 fps on NVIDIA 3090 with 2D neural rendering module [S21].
 *   **Strengths:** Handles view-dependent effects, high-quality novel view synthesis, fine details [S13].
